 middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, November to December finished at 44% of normal on the middle of the grids, and August to September at 57%. This year so far, January to February 2026 sits at 24% of normal and June to July 2026 at 164%. Grid 20869 has a preliminary estimate of 84.7 for August to September 2026.</p>"}
